<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="description" content="<%= description %>" />
  <title><%= title %> &middot; Compliance Sphere</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg?v=<%= typeof assetVersion !== 'undefined' ? assetVersion : '0' %>" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/public.css?v=<%= typeof assetVersion !== 'undefined' ? assetVersion : '0' %>" />
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#mainContent">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Compliance Sphere home">
      <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 22 22" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="9.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/>
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/>
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="2.5" fill="currentColor"/>
      </svg>
      <span>Compliance Sphere</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Public navigation">
      <a href="/security"<%= page === 'security' ? ' aria-current="page"' : '' %>>Security</a>
      <a href="/privacy"<%= page === 'privacy' ? ' aria-current="page"' : '' %>>Privacy</a>
      <a href="/terms"<%= page === 'terms' ? ' aria-current="page"' : '' %>>Terms</a>
      <a class="nav-sign-in" href="/login">Sign in</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="mainContent">
    <% if (page === 'home') { %>
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Multi-framework assurance delivery</p>
        <h1>Four standards. One evidence base. Four separate conclusions.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Compliance Sphere is the delivery record consulting firms run an engagement on. Assessments, evidence, findings, approvals and reports live against one client, and each framework still reaches its own conclusion on its own method.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="<%= evaluationUrl %>">Request an evaluation</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/login">Sign in</a>
        </div>
        <p class="plain-note">Evaluation access is issued by invitation. No unscoped self-sign-up.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section bordered" aria-labelledby="programmesTitle">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Programme register</p>
          <h2 id="programmesTitle">A shared operating record, not a certification shortcut.</h2>
          <p class="section-note">A conclusion is a readiness position for a stated boundary and date. It is the consulting firm's assessment, and it does not stand in for a certification body's audit decision.</p>
        </div>
        <table class="register">
          <caption>Catalogues carried in the product</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Programme</th><th scope="col">Catalogue</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% programmes.forEach(function (p) { %>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span class="code"><%= p.code %></span>
                <span class="name"><%= p.formalName %></span>
                <span class="desc"><%= p.descriptor %></span>
              </td>
              <td>
                <span class="count"><%= p.count %></span>
                <span class="unit"><%= p.unit %></span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <% }); %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="governedTitle">
        <p class="eyebrow">What governed means here</p>
        <h2 id="governedTitle">The record resists being talked into a better answer.</h2>
        <p class="claim">Most of this product is refusals. A conclusion that is not supported cannot be recorded, an approved report cannot be edited afterwards, and the person who proposes a decision is not the person who signs it off.</p>
        <div class="mechanisms">
          <div>
            <h3>A conclusion needs evidence attached</h3>
            <p>Controls and obligations are concluded against linked evidence, not against a dropdown. Coverage is reported separately from sufficiency, so one retained file is never mistaken for a complete evidence set.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Approved records freeze</h3>
            <p>An approved report is a content-addressed snapshot. Reassessment opens a new record rather than rewriting the old one, so what the client was told in March still reads in March's terms.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Recommending is not deciding</h3>
            <p>On third-party risk the consultancy records a recommendation and the client's decision authority accepts or declines it. The two are stored separately and export as separate columns.</p>
            <span class="ref">Maker-checker applies to the recommendation itself.</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Catalogues are fixed at a version</h3>
            <p>Each framework catalogue carries a content hash and validates itself on load. An engagement states which release it was assessed against, and a later release supersedes rather than silently replaces it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section bordered" aria-labelledby="rolesTitle">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Role separation</p>
          <h2 id="rolesTitle">One engagement, four bounded views.</h2>
          <p class="section-note">Membership is checked on every protected action. A client team sees the workspaces assigned to it and nothing adjacent.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="roles">
          <div><strong>Consultant</strong><span>Runs fieldwork, links evidence, maintains workpapers and drafts controlled outputs.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Manager</strong><span>Holds access and approval. Reviews decisions, signs off governed records, sees the firm portfolio.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Client team</strong><span>Answers requests, supplies evidence and follows progress on its own engagement only.</span></div>
          <div><strong>External auditor</strong><span>Reaches a time-boxed, token-scoped view of approved records without an account on the firm.</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section evaluation" aria-labelledby="evaluationTitle">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A useful evaluation</p>
          <h2 id="evaluationTitle">Try to break the boundary.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="claim">An evaluation runs in an isolated workspace. The useful test is not whether a report renders. It is whether you can conclude a control with no evidence behind it, edit a report after approval, approve your own recommendation, or see a client that was never assigned to you.</p>
          <p class="section-note">If any of those succeed, we would rather hear it from you than from an auditor.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="<%= evaluationUrl %>">Request an evaluation</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="/security">Read the security overview</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    <% } else if (page === 'access') { %>
      <section class="prose-page">
        <p class="eyebrow">Controlled access</p>
        <h1>Access starts with an invitation.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Self-sign-up is disabled. Each account must be assigned to the correct consulting firm or client workspace before it can sign in.</p>
        <% if (typeof accessNotice !== 'undefined' && accessNotice) { %><p class="notice" role="status"><%= accessNotice %></p><% } %>
        <h2>What happens next</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Request an evaluation or contact the person who shared this site.</li>
          <li>An administrator creates the appropriate role and sends a single-use invitation.</li>
          <li>You set your password and enter only the workspace assigned to you.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="<%= evaluationUrl %>">Request an evaluation</a><a class="button secondary" href="/login">I already have access</a></div>
      </section>
    <% } else if (page === 'security') { %>
      <section class="prose-page">
        <p class="eyebrow">Security overview</p>
        <h1>Security boundaries should be testable.</h1>
        <p class="lede">The product implements application controls for tenant separation, role-restricted actions, governed records and external sharing. The operating organization remains responsible for secure configuration, infrastructure and monitoring.</p>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <article><h2>Identity and access</h2><p>Accounts are invitation-only. Firm and workspace membership are checked on protected actions, sensitive administration is permission-gated, and password reset or account deactivation invalidates existing sessions.</p></article>
          <article><h2>Application protection</h2><p>State-changing browser requests use CSRF protection. Session cookies are HTTP-only and SameSite-protected, with secure cookies required in production. Controlled document HTML is sanitized before display.</p></article>
          <article><h2>External sharing</h2><p>Auditor links use high-entropy tokens stored as hashes. Shared document views are limited to approved or published records and sanitize controlled content.</p></article>
          <article><h2>Records and evidence</h2><p>Governed versions, review decisions and audit events preserve decision history. Production upload processing requires malware scanning when deployed with the documented configuration.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="caveat"><strong>Deployment evidence matters.</strong><p>Encryption keys, TLS, backups, malware-scanner health, logging, patching and infrastructure access depend on the operator's deployment. Ask the operator to demonstrate these controls for the environment you will use.</p></div>
        <h2>Report a security issue</h2>
        <% if (securityEmail) { %>
          <p>Email <a href="mailto:<%= securityEmail %>?subject=Security%20report"><%= securityEmail %></a>. Do not include live secrets or personal data in the first message.</p>
        <% } else { %>
          <p>Use the <a href="/contact?topic=security">security contact path</a> or contact the organization that gave you access. Do not include live secrets or personal data in the first message.</p>
        <% } %>
        <p>A machine-readable disclosure contact is available at <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a>.</p>
      </section>
    <% } else if (page === 'privacy') { %>
      <section class="prose-page">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy responsibilities are shared with the operator.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Compliance Sphere is deployed for an organization. That organization determines why workspace data is processed and should provide the privacy notice, retention schedule and contact applicable to its deployment.</p>
        <h2>Data the service may process</h2>
        <ul><li>Account, firm, workspace and role information.</li><li>Assessment responses, requests, evidence, documents, findings, comments and approvals.</li><li>Security and audit records such as sign-in activity, actor, action and timestamp.</li><li>Files deliberately uploaded by authorized users.</li></ul>
        <h2>Browser storage</h2>
        <p>Essential cookies maintain authenticated sessions and request protection. The interface may store display preferences and campaign parameters in your browser; it does not need to send those optional values to a third-party analytics service.</p>
        <h2>Retention and rights</h2>
        <p>Retention, access, correction, export and deletion handling are set by the operating organization and may be limited by contractual, legal or audit-record obligations. Contact that organization for a request relating to your data.</p>
        <p><a href="/contact?topic=privacy">Find the appropriate contact</a>.</p>
      </section>
    <% } else if (page === 'terms') { %>
      <section class="prose-page">
        <p class="eyebrow">Terms of use</p>
        <h1>Use the service only within your authorization.</h1>
        <p class="lede">These product-level terms support evaluation and authorized use. The contract and policies of the organization operating your deployment also apply and take precedence where required.</p>
        <h2>Authorized use</h2>
        <p>Use only the account, firm, client workspace and records assigned to you. Do not share invitations, passwords or external-access links, and do not upload material you are not permitted to process.</p>
        <h2>Security testing</h2>
        <p>Do not probe, scan, disrupt or attempt to bypass controls unless the operating organization has given you written authorization defining the target and test window. Report suspected vulnerabilities through the <a href="/security">security page</a>.</p>
        <h2>No certification or professional-advice claim</h2>
        <p>The software helps organize GRC work. Its use does not itself certify conformity, guarantee security, replace professional judgment or constitute legal advice.</p>
        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>Evaluation environments may change or be withdrawn. The operator is responsible for service commitments, data recovery and notice of material terms applicable to its users.</p>
      </section>
    <% } else if (page === 'contact') { %>
      <section class="prose-page">
        <p class="eyebrow"><%= topic === 'security' ? 'Security contact' : topic === 'privacy' ? 'Privacy contact' : 'Evaluation request' %></p>
        <h1><%= topic === 'security' ? 'Report a security concern.' : topic === 'privacy' ? 'Contact the deployment operator.' : 'Start with the workflow you need to test.' %></h1>
        <% if (topic === 'security') { %>
          <p class="lede">Describe the affected page, observed behaviour and a safe way to reproduce it. Do not send passwords, access tokens, production evidence or unnecessary personal data.</p>
        <% } else if (topic === 'privacy') { %>
          <p class="lede">The organization operating this deployment handles privacy requests for its users and workspace data.</p>
        <% } else { %>
          <p class="lede">A useful evaluation should include your target framework, expected roles, critical evidence flow and the security review your team intends to perform.</p>
        <% } %>
        <% if (evaluationUrl !== '/contact' && topic === 'evaluation') { %>
          <a class="button primary" href="<%= evaluationUrl %>">Open the evaluation request</a>
        <% } else if ((topic === 'security' ? securityEmail : contactEmail)) { const email = topic === 'security' ? securityEmail : contactEmail; %>
          <a class="button primary" href="mailto:<%= email %>?subject=<%= topic === 'security' ? 'Security%20report' : topic === 'privacy' ? 'Privacy%20request' : 'Compliance%20Sphere%20evaluation' %>">Email <%= email %></a>
        <% } else { %>
          <div class="caveat"><strong>No public contact has been configured for this deployment.</strong><p>Reply to the person who shared this address or contact the organization operating the site. Ask them to configure the appropriate evaluation, privacy or security contact before external use.</p></div>
        <% } %>
        <% if (topic === 'security') { %><p>Read the <a href="/security">security overview</a> before submitting a report.</p><% } %>
      </section>
    <% } %>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <span>&copy; <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> Compliance Sphere</span>
    <nav aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href="/security">Security</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a></nav>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
